    {
      "method": "on_withdraw_complete",
      "whoMayCall": "the contract itself only (#[private], restricted to current_account_id as a cross-contract callback)"
    },
    {
      "method": "new",
      "whoMayCall": "anyone, but only once at initial deployment while the account has no contract state; sets owner and starts unpaused with an empty balances map"
    }
  ],
  "standingNote": "NEAR enters via deposit, sits as bookkeeping in the balances map while the real NEAR rests on the contract's own account, and leaves via withdraw's Promise::transfer, with on_withdraw_complete restoring the balance if a transfer fails. In this code the owner can only pause deposits — there is no in-code path for the owner to move users' funds, and withdrawals are never pausable — but that guarantee holds only for this exact code: key and upgrade control has to be checked on the deployed account (full-access or function-call keys on the account, who can redeploy/upgrade the WASM, and whether the owner is an EOA or a contract), because anyone who can upgrade the code or sign for the account could bypass the balances map and drain the pot holding all deposits. Also note the pause flag lives in mutable state and the owner can be set arbitrarily at init, so confirm the deployed instance's owner value as well."
}

